# =============================================================================
# provider box configuration — copy to .env and fill in.
# =============================================================================
# .env is gitignored. Five files are rendered from it by ./render.sh:
# provider.toml (A SECRET), connector.toml, operator-bearer.token,
# operator-write.keys and nginx/conf.d/node.conf.
#
# Everything that makes a box YOURS lives in .env and in the listings file it
# names, both gitignored, so the checkout itself stays unmodified and
# auto-apply.sh can keep fast-forwarding it. Never edit a committed template.
#
# ── SINGLE-QUOTE ANYTHING WITH A SPACE OR A BRACE ────────────────────────────
# This file is read twice, by two parsers. docker compose reads it itself, and
# ./render.sh and ./bootstrap.sh `source` it as shell — where an unquoted value
# with a space runs its second word as a command, and an unquoted `{"a":"b"}`
# loses its quotes and stops being JSON. Single quotes satisfy both: compose
# strips them, and the shell takes the value whole.

# ── Required ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# The zone this box's hostnames live under. Two A-records must point here:
#   proxy.provider.${DOMAIN}   the paid ILP edge
#   provider.${DOMAIN}         GET /health, and nothing else
# Not used, and best left empty, on a hidden box (HIDDEN=1, below).
DOMAIN=

# This box's PUBLIC IPv4. It is where tenants reach their workloads — the
# daemon publishes each lease's SSH forward and its sixteen ports on it — and
# it is published in the Provider Profile. A container address here is a
# provider nobody can use. Never rendered on a hidden box (HIDDEN=1, below),
# which publishes no address at all.
PUBLIC_IP=

# What the Profile calls this provider. Free text, shown in a directory.
PROVIDER_NAME=''

# This provider's own ILP address. Every route it sells hangs off it
# (<ILP_ADDRESS>.<tier>.v1.spawn, <ILP_ADDRESS>.status, ...), and the
# connector answers for it. No default: pick one of your own, e.g.
# g.<your-name>.provider. render.sh refuses anything under `g.toon.` — the
# TOON fleet's own namespace — unless TOON_DEVNET_BOX=1, below.
ILP_ADDRESS=

# What this provider sells: a TOML file of [[listings]], yours and gitignored.
# Start from the example (the TOON devnet provider's own tiers):
#   cp listings.example.toml listings.toml
# render.sh splices it into provider.toml and generates the connector's routes
# from the result. A path relative to this directory.
LISTINGS_FILE=listings.toml

# ── THIS PROVIDER'S IDENTITY ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 64 hex characters:
#   openssl rand -hex 32
#
# It signs the Profile, every Listing, every Liveness and every Eviction
# Notice, and it is the key a Lease Request is addressed to. It goes INLINE
# into the rendered provider.toml — which is why that file is 0600 and
# gitignored, unlike every other rendered config in this fleet.
#
# Changing it makes this a different provider: a new pubkey, an empty
# directory entry, and every tenant holding a lease addressed to the old one
# left talking to nobody. Record it somewhere off this box.
NOSTR_PRIVATE_KEY=

# =============================================================================
# THE TOON DEVNET PRESET — the relay and the settlement chains
# =============================================================================
# Where this provider is listed and what it is paid in. Every value below is
# the TOON devnet's: its relay, and mock USDC on Base Sepolia and on Solana
# devnet — test money, so a provider on this preset earns nothing real. Keep
# the block as-is to join the devnet; to settle elsewhere, change the block as
# a whole: the relay's write route and each token are facts about the network,
# not preferences.
#
# The settlement values are rendered into BOTH provider.toml's [[settlement]]
# (what the Profile tells a tenant it can pay with) and connector.toml's
# [settlement.*] (what the connector verifies claims against), from this one
# copy. The connector proves each against a live chain at boot: a wrong
# address is a refuse-to-start, not a mispriced node.

# ── The relay (devnet preset) ────────────────────────────────────────────────

# The relay READ url this provider publishes to and names in its Profile. A
# tenant reads the directory here; this provider also searches it for Blob
# Records by digest, which is how an image named by digest alone resolves.
RELAY_WS=wss://relay-ws.devnet.toonprotocol.dev

# The same relay's client edge, where its PAID write route is bought. The
# publisher opens a channel against this node and pays it per write.
RELAY_EDGE_URL=https://proxy.relay.devnet.toonprotocol.dev

# Relay READ url -> the PAID ILP destination that writes to it. JSON. Never a
# `.ephemeral` destination: the free lane's rate limit is keyed by remote
# address and shared by everyone behind one connector, and directory events
# are paid replaceable events (ADR 0007). The publisher refuses to start if
# this names one.
RELAY_WRITE_ROUTES='{"wss://relay-ws.devnet.toonprotocol.dev":"g.toon.relay"}'

# ── Settlement: Base Sepolia (devnet preset) ──────────────────────────────────
# The EVM chain id, published as `evm:<id>`; it must be the chain the RPC
# answers for.
SETTLEMENT_EVM_CHAIN_ID=84532
SETTLEMENT_EVM_RPC_URL=https://base-sepolia-rpc.publicnode.com
# The TokenNetworkRegistry, not a token network: the connector resolves the
# network through it at boot, so a redeployed network needs no edit here.
SETTLEMENT_EVM_REGISTRY=0x0c41D9D424d6B075A3cEa1068a694f7847a8CCa5
# Mock USDC. Its decimals must be what the token's own decimals() answers.
SETTLEMENT_EVM_TOKEN=0x49beE1Bca5d15Fb0963117923403F9498119a9Ce
SETTLEMENT_EVM_DECIMALS=6

# ── Settlement: Solana devnet (devnet preset) ─────────────────────────────────
SETTLEMENT_SOLANA_RPC_URL=https://api.devnet.solana.com
SETTLEMENT_SOLANA_PROGRAM_ID=2aEVJ8koKD8LTZrLRSGtAtU7LBt4e7QjjCgf1kzQ7Rip
# Mock USDC.
SETTLEMENT_SOLANA_TOKEN=34eSxY7qxQ4GzyhDJ8GpUcTz1WWzruGbJbR8q6TtxfQU
SETTLEMENT_SOLANA_DECIMALS=6

# =============================================================================
# End of the devnet preset.
# =============================================================================

# ── The wallet that pays for relay writes ────────────────────────────────────
# A BIP-39 phrase, and ITS OWN, shared with nothing: two payers on one channel
# share one nonce watermark, and the loser of that race has every later claim
# refused. It holds money and never identity — it cannot forge a directory
# event, only decline to pay for one.
#
# Fund the Solana address it derives with devnet SOL and mock USDC; see
# README.md § "The two funded identities".
PUBLISHER_MNEMONIC=''

# Where Let's Encrypt sends expiry warnings.
LETSENCRYPT_EMAIL=you@example.com

# Leave at 1 until DNS resolves to this box, then set 0 and re-run
# ./init-letsencrypt.sh. Staging certificates are untrusted by browsers but do
# not burn the production rate limit while you are still wiring DNS up.
LETSENCRYPT_STAGING=1

# ── The operator surface's two credentials ───────────────────────────────────

# Gates the connector's /metrics and redeem endpoints — which also means it is
# how this provider's earnings are redeemed, so it is not optional in practice.
#   openssl rand -hex 32
OPERATOR_BEARER_TOKEN=

# The ED25519 PUBLIC key permitted to sign operator writes — 64 hex
# characters, and NOT a nostr npub, a secp256k1 key or base58. Generate the
# private half OFF THIS BOX and keep it there:
#
#   openssl rand -hex 32 > operator-write.key    # keep this elsewhere
#   docker run --rm -v "$PWD:/d:ro" \
#     ghcr.io/toon-protocol/connector:rust-2026.09.11.1 \
#     send --operator-key /d/operator-write.key --print-keyid
#
# Revoke a key by changing this line, re-rendering and restarting.
OPERATOR_WRITE_KEY=

# =============================================================================
# RUNNING HIDDEN — a Hidden Provider, reached only through Anyone (optional)
# =============================================================================
# README.md § "Running hidden" first: a hidden box needs its OWN settlement
# RPC nodes, which is the heavy part. Uncomment the four lines together.
#
# The switch, and the compose overlay that goes with it. They are two lines
# because docker compose reads COMPOSE_FILE itself; render.sh refuses a .env
# where they disagree.
# HIDDEN=1
# COMPOSE_FILE=docker-compose.yml:docker-compose.hidden.yml
#
# The settlement RPC nodes THIS BOX RUNS ITSELF, one per chain the connector
# settles on. They replace SETTLEMENT_EVM_RPC_URL and SETTLEMENT_SOLANA_RPC_URL
# above, which stay as they are. Each must be on a private address the
# connector's container can route to: 10/8, 172.16/12, 192.168/16, or a name
# resolving only to those. A public RPC is refused, because the connector
# dials it directly and would link this box's address to its settlement keys;
# loopback is refused too, because inside the container 127.0.0.1 is the
# container. The Solana one is also what the Profile's hiding claim names
# (`anon.settlement_rpc_url`).
# HIDDEN_SETTLEMENT_EVM_RPC_URL=http://10.0.0.5:8545
# HIDDEN_SETTLEMENT_SOLANA_RPC_URL=http://10.0.0.5:8899

# ── Written by bootstrap.sh; do not fill in by hand ──────────────────────────

# This box's connector's own sealing key, copied verbatim from
# `GET /ilp/identity` INCLUDING the `0x`. A tenant compares it byte for byte
# against what the connector answers and refuses to spawn if they differ
# (ADR 0011), so it is a COPY OF A FACT and not a setting. bootstrap.sh starts
# the connector, reads it and appends it here, which is the only way to get it
# right without transcribing a 130-character hex string.
#
# Re-generate signer.key and you must delete this line and re-run bootstrap.sh.
# CONNECTOR_SEAL_KEY=

# HIDDEN=1 only: this box's own `.anyone` address, copied from the anon
# daemon's hidden_service/hostname. The connector is reached there and nowhere
# else, and both rendered configs name it. A COPY OF A FACT, like the sealing
# key: bootstrap.sh reads it and appends it here. The key behind it is on the
# anon_data volume; lose that volume and the address changes, and bootstrap.sh
# refuses until you restore the volume or delete this line.
# HIDDEN_ADDRESS=

# ── Optional ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ONLY the TOON fleet's own boxes set this. It lets ILP_ADDRESS sit under
# `g.toon.`, the fleet's namespace; anyone else doing so would answer for the
# fleet's routes and take payment meant for another box. The devnet provider
# box sets TOON_DEVNET_BOX=1, ILP_ADDRESS=g.toon.provider and
# LISTINGS_FILE=listings.example.toml, so that its tiers stay a reviewed commit.
# TOON_DEVNET_BOX=1

# The branch this box follows. `auto-apply.sh` fast-forwards it every five
# minutes and applies what it finds. Leave it at `main`: nothing an operator
# customises is a committed file, so there is nothing to fork for. It is a
# variable because the devnet provider runs ahead of `main` while a milestone
# is unmerged.
# TRACK_BRANCH=main

# The Solana RPC the publisher settles against. On a hidden box the publisher
# dials it through anon unless it is on a private address, so pointing it at
# HIDDEN_SETTLEMENT_SOLANA_RPC_URL's node keeps it off the Anyone network too.
# SOLANA_RPC_URL=https://api.devnet.solana.com

# An existing certificate lineage to keep using, if this box already has one
# filed under a different name. Defaults to proxy.provider.${DOMAIN}.
# CERT_NAME=
